// Path-addressed twin of ../+page.marko: /create/preview/<item>.
//
// This route exists ONLY so the static build can emit one document per
// showcase item. The parent page selects its entire body from the `item`
// value at RENDER time, and a static host cannot serve a different file per
// query string — so `?item=preview-page-2` and `?item=preview-page-3` would
// otherwise both collapse onto the single /create/preview document and
// silently serve preview-page-1. That would break 32 of the 48 gallery
// baselines while every test still "passed".
//
// The canonical public URL is still /create/preview?item=<item> (what the
// customizer iframe and e2e/gallery-visual.spec.ts both request); the Worker
// rewrites that onto this path. Rendering the parent page here — rather than
// copying it — is what guarantees the two spellings can never drift apart:
// ../+page.marko reads `$global.params.item` in preference to the query
// string, so it renders the right body under either URL.
import PreviewPage from "../+page.marko";

<PreviewPage/>
